error[L0263]: cannot borrow `copy.lo` as mutable more than once at a time (E0499)
  --> tests/corpus/reject/overlapping_arguments.lc:40:26
   |
40 |     settle(&mut copy.lo, &mut copy.lo); //~ error: L0263 cannot borrow `copy.lo` as mutable more than once at a time (E0499)
   |            ------------  ^^^^^^^^^^^^
   |            |
   |            `copy.lo` is lent here, for the whole call
   |
   = note: the arguments of one call are evaluated left to right, and a lend lasts until the call returns: two arguments may not name overlapping places when either is lent by `&mut`, and a value lent by `&` is not moved, as rustc rules
